{
  "name": "workboard",
  "version": "0.0.0",
  "private": true,
  "type": "module",
  "scripts": {
    "start": "node server.js",
    "test": "node --test"
  }
}
# Workboard

Requires Node.js 22.22.1. No packages need to be installed.

```sh
npm start
```

The server binds to `0.0.0.0:8080` by default. Configure the port and persistent SQLite database path with:

```sh
PORT=8080 DB_PATH=./data/workboard.sqlite npm start
```

Open `/` to create and open projects. `GET /health` returns `{"status":"ok"}`.

On a project page, create tasks, toggle their completion checkboxes, and use
`Task filter` to view All, Open, Completed, or Deleted tasks. Projects and tasks persist
in the configured SQLite file across server restarts.

Use `Project filter` to switch between Active and Archived projects. Project
rows show completion totals and let you archive or restore a project. Archived
projects remain readable with working task filters; task creation and completion
changes are disabled until restoration. Existing databases migrate automatically.

Use `New project name` and `Rename project` on an active project page to rename
it. Names are trimmed and required. Renaming preserves the project's URL,
creation order, tasks, and completion totals. Archived projects must be restored
before they can be renamed.

Each task row provides `New task title` and `Rename task`. Titles are trimmed
and required. Renaming preserves task ownership, creation order, completion,
filter membership, and project completion totals. Archived projects disable
task renaming until restoration. Renamed titles persist across server restarts.

Each task row has a `Task priority` selector with Low, Normal, and High options.
Existing tasks default to Normal when migrating from databases without priorities.
Priorities persist independently across
reloads and restarts, including after renaming, archiving, and restoration.
Archived projects disable priority edits until restoration.

Use `Priority filter` (All, Low, Normal, High) together with `Task filter` to
show tasks matching both selections in creation order. Both filters stay selected
through task edits, including when an edited task no longer matches. Filters work
on archived projects and never change saved data or completion totals. Opening
a project from the project list starts both filters at All.

Use `Default task priority` (Low, Normal, High) on each project page to choose
the priority for subsequent tasks. Each project starts at Normal. Changing the
default preserves existing tasks and both selected filters. Defaults persist
independently across reloads, restarts, renaming, archiving, and restoration.
Archived projects show the saved default but disable changes until restoration.

Each task row has a `Task due date` textbox and `Save due date` button.
Save a real Gregorian date in YYYY-MM-DD format (years 0001–9999), or save
an empty value to clear it. Surrounding whitespace is trimmed. Invalid dates
show an alert and preserve the saved date. Dates persist as calendar days,
independently of timezones, and preserve all other task data and both filters.
Archived projects disable date edits until restoration.

Use `Due from`, `Due through`, and `Apply due range` to filter by inclusive
calendar-date boundaries alongside completion and priority. Blank boundaries
are unbounded; undated tasks match only when both boundaries are blank.
Invalid dates or reversed ranges show an alert and retain the applied range.
Edits and filter changes retain the range, and archived projects allow range
filtering. Opening a project from the list starts with empty range boundaries.
Filtering never changes saved task data or the all-task completion summary.

Each task row provides `Destination project` and `Move task` to move it to
another active project. Destinations use current project names in project
creation order. First visits append after all positions established in the
destination; returning tasks resume their remembered position in that project.
Positions are saved independently for each project, even while a task is away,
and survive restarts, project renaming, archival and restoration. Moves preserve
title, completion, priority and due date, and retain the source page's filters.
Both completion summaries reflect the new ownership. Task order and ownership
persist across restarts. Archived projects cannot send or receive tasks; move
controls are also disabled when there are no eligible destinations.

Run the integration checks with:

```sh
npm test
```

Use `Project search` and `Search projects` to match project names within the
selected Active or Archived list. Use `Task search` and `Search tasks` to match
titles alongside completion, priority and due-range filters. Searches ignore
ASCII letter case and trim surrounding query whitespace. Runs of ASCII spaces
and horizontal tabs in queries and names/titles match as one space, without
rewriting saved or displayed text. Other internal whitespace remains literal.
Blank queries match all rows allowed by the other filters.
Task edits and moves retain the applied search and filters. Searches work on
archived projects and do not change stored data or all-task summaries. Opening
a project from the list, or returning via `Projects`, starts with an empty query.

Each task row has a multiline `Task notes` textarea and `Save notes` button.
Notes are saved as plain text, preserving whitespace, line breaks, Unicode and
literal markup. Empty text clears notes. Existing and new tasks start with empty
notes. Notes persist across reloads, restarts, renaming, moves and remembered
return positions, without changing other task data or the selected filters.
Searches continue to match only project names and task titles. Archived projects
display saved notes with editing disabled until restoration.

Live task rows provide `Delete task`. Deleted tasks keep all fields and remembered
positions, but leave the live lists and completion summaries. Select `Deleted`
to read them using the same priority, date and title filters, then `Restore task`
to return them to their reserved positions. Deleted task editing and movement
are disabled until restoration. Archived projects disable deletion and restoration
while keeping filters usable. Deletion persists across restarts; upgrades preserve
existing tasks as live.

Use `Download project` on any project page to download UTF-8 JSON named
`workboard-project.json` (format `workboard-project`, version 1). The document
contains the project's name, archive state and default priority, plus all its
live and deleted tasks in stored order with title, completion, explicit priority,
due date, notes and deletion state. Downloads ignore the selected filters and
search, and leave all saved data and page selections unchanged. Exported notes
use LF line endings without rewriting the stored notes. Archived and empty
projects can also be downloaded.

On the home page, paste a version 1 portable document into `Project JSON`, enter
an `Imported project name`, and select `Import project`. The override name is
trimmed and required. The complete document is validated before a single
transaction creates a new independent project and opens it. Invalid documents
show `Invalid project JSON`, retain both inputs, and leave existing data unchanged.
Imports retain archive state, default priority, task order, exact titles,
completion, explicit priorities, dates, notes (with LF line endings), and deletion
state. Internal identities are always newly allocated. Deleted tasks retain their
reserved positions for restoration and later moves/returns. Archived imports
remain read-only until restored.

Select `Task directory` on the home page to read tasks across projects. Each
opening starts with Active project scope, All task and priority filters, and
empty search and due range. Scope, live/deleted status, priority, inclusive date
range and normalized title search intersect without changing saved data. Results
follow project creation order and each project's stored task order, and show the
original title, owner name, completion, priority, due date and literal notes.
Directory rows contain no task editing controls. `Open project` opens the owner
with default project filters, including archived owners; `Projects` returns home.
Imported and upgraded tasks appear with their saved fields and public defaults.

Use `Complete visible tasks` or `Reopen visible tasks` in the directory to update
all matching live tasks across active projects. Current filters, search and due
range remain selected; results and project summaries reflect the saved completion
state. Each action is disabled when no visible task needs that change, and both
are disabled for Archived scope or Deleted tasks. Other fields and remembered
positions remain unchanged. Empty resolved results show `No matching tasks`;
the announcement is hidden while a new directory page is loading.

Use `Directory order` to view results in Original, Priority (High first), Due date
(earliest first, undated last), or Title order. Title ordering folds only ASCII
uppercase letters and compares Unicode code points, preserving literal internal
whitespace. Ties retain original project/task order. The selection stays through
filtering, searches, date ranges and bulk actions; each new directory opening
starts at Original. Ordering never changes stored order, exports or remembered
return positions.
import http from 'node:http';
import { DatabaseSync } from 'node:sqlite';
import { mkdirSync } from 'node:fs';
import { dirname } from 'node:path';

const dbPath = process.env.DB_PATH || 'data/workboard.sqlite';
mkdirSync(dirname(dbPath), { recursive: true });
const db = new DatabaseSync(dbPath);
db.exec(`CREATE TABLE IF NOT EXISTS projects (
  id INTEGER PRIMARY KEY AUTOINCREMENT,
  name TEXT NOT NULL
)`);
if (!db.prepare('PRAGMA table_info(projects)').all().some((column) => column.name === 'archived')) {
  db.exec('ALTER TABLE projects ADD COLUMN archived INTEGER NOT NULL DEFAULT 0 CHECK (archived IN (0, 1))');
}
if (!db.prepare('PRAGMA table_info(projects)').all().some((column) => column.name === 'default_priority')) {
  db.exec("ALTER TABLE projects ADD COLUMN default_priority TEXT NOT NULL DEFAULT 'Normal' CHECK (default_priority IN ('Low', 'Normal', 'High'))");
}
const findProject = db.prepare('SELECT id, name, archived, default_priority FROM projects WHERE id = ?');
const createProject = db.prepare('INSERT INTO projects (name) VALUES (?)');
const setProjectArchived = db.prepare('UPDATE projects SET archived = ? WHERE id = ?');
const renameProject = db.prepare('UPDATE projects SET name = ? WHERE id = ?');
const setDefaultPriority = db.prepare('UPDATE projects SET default_priority = ? WHERE id = ?');
db.exec(`PRAGMA foreign_keys = ON;
CREATE TABLE IF NOT EXISTS tasks (
  id INTEGER PRIMARY KEY AUTOINCREMENT,
  project_id INTEGER NOT NULL REFERENCES projects(id),
  title TEXT NOT NULL,
  completed INTEGER NOT NULL DEFAULT 0 CHECK (completed IN (0, 1))
)`);
if (!db.prepare('PRAGMA table_info(tasks)').all().some((column) => column.name === 'priority')) {
  db.exec("ALTER TABLE tasks ADD COLUMN priority TEXT NOT NULL DEFAULT 'Normal' CHECK (priority IN ('Low', 'Normal', 'High'))");
}
if (!db.prepare('PRAGMA table_info(tasks)').all().some((column) => column.name === 'due_date')) {
  db.exec("ALTER TABLE tasks ADD COLUMN due_date TEXT NOT NULL DEFAULT ''");
}
if (!db.prepare('PRAGMA table_info(tasks)').all().some((column) => column.name === 'notes')) {
  db.exec("ALTER TABLE tasks ADD COLUMN notes TEXT NOT NULL DEFAULT ''");
}
if (!db.prepare('PRAGMA table_info(tasks)').all().some((column) => column.name === 'deleted')) {
  db.exec('ALTER TABLE tasks ADD COLUMN deleted INTEGER NOT NULL DEFAULT 0 CHECK (deleted IN (0, 1))');
}
if (!db.prepare('PRAGMA table_info(tasks)').all().some((column) => column.name === 'position')) {
  db.exec('ALTER TABLE tasks ADD COLUMN position INTEGER NOT NULL DEFAULT 0; UPDATE tasks SET position = id');
}
// Keep positions even while tasks are away, so returns never depend on move order.
// Seed the current positions when upgrading an existing database.
db.exec(`CREATE TABLE IF NOT EXISTS task_positions (
  task_id INTEGER NOT NULL REFERENCES tasks(id),
  project_id INTEGER NOT NULL REFERENCES projects(id),
  position INTEGER NOT NULL,
  PRIMARY KEY (task_id, project_id)
);
INSERT OR IGNORE INTO task_positions (task_id, project_id, position)
  SELECT id, project_id, position FROM tasks`);
const listProjects = db.prepare(`SELECT p.id, p.name, p.archived,
  COUNT(t.id) AS total, COALESCE(SUM(t.completed), 0) AS completed
  FROM projects p LEFT JOIN tasks t ON t.project_id = p.id AND t.deleted = 0
  WHERE p.archived = ? GROUP BY p.id ORDER BY p.id`);
const listTasks = db.prepare('SELECT id, title, completed, priority, due_date, notes, deleted FROM tasks WHERE project_id = ? ORDER BY position, id');
const listDirectoryTasks = db.prepare(`SELECT t.*, p.name AS project_name
  FROM tasks t JOIN projects p ON p.id = t.project_id
  WHERE p.archived = ? ORDER BY p.id, t.position, t.id`);
const insertTask = db.prepare('INSERT INTO tasks (project_id, title, priority, position) VALUES (?, ?, ?, ?)');
const nextPosition = db.prepare('SELECT COALESCE(MAX(position), 0) + 1 AS position FROM task_positions WHERE project_id = ?');
const rememberPosition = db.prepare('INSERT INTO task_positions (task_id, project_id, position) VALUES (?, ?, ?)');
const rememberedPosition = db.prepare('SELECT position FROM task_positions WHERE task_id = ? AND project_id = ?');
const destinations = db.prepare('SELECT id, name FROM projects WHERE archived = 0 AND id != ? ORDER BY id');
const updateTaskProject = db.prepare('UPDATE tasks SET project_id = ?, position = ? WHERE id = ? AND project_id = ?');
const updateTask = db.prepare('UPDATE tasks SET completed = ? WHERE id = ? AND project_id = ?');
const findTask = db.prepare('SELECT id, deleted FROM tasks WHERE id = ? AND project_id = ?');
const renameTask = db.prepare('UPDATE tasks SET title = ? WHERE id = ? AND project_id = ?');
const setTaskPriority = db.prepare('UPDATE tasks SET priority = ? WHERE id = ? AND project_id = ?');
const setTaskDueDate = db.prepare('UPDATE tasks SET due_date = ? WHERE id = ? AND project_id = ?');
const setTaskDeleted = db.prepare('UPDATE tasks SET deleted = ? WHERE id = ? AND project_id = ?');
const setTaskNotes = db.prepare('UPDATE tasks SET notes = ? WHERE id = ? AND project_id = ?');

function transaction(work) {
  db.exec('BEGIN IMMEDIATE');
  try {
    work();
    db.exec('COMMIT');
  } catch (error) {
    db.exec('ROLLBACK');
    throw error;
  }
}

function createTask(projectId, title, priority) {
  transaction(() => {
    const { position } = nextPosition.get(projectId);
    const { lastInsertRowid } = insertTask.run(projectId, title, priority, position);
    rememberPosition.run(lastInsertRowid, projectId, position);
  });
}

function moveTask(destinationId, taskId, sourceId) {
  transaction(() => {
    let saved = rememberedPosition.get(taskId, destinationId);
    if (!saved) {
      saved = nextPosition.get(destinationId);
      rememberPosition.run(taskId, destinationId, saved.position);
    }
    updateTaskProject.run(destinationId, saved.position, taskId, sourceId);
  });
}

// Validate calendar components directly; dates are never converted to timestamps.
function validDueDate(value) {
  if (!/^[0-9]{4}-[0-9]{2}-[0-9]{2}$/.test(value)) return false;
  const [year, month, day] = value.split('-').map(Number);
  if (year < 1 || month < 1 || month > 12) return false;
  const leap = year % 4 === 0 && (year % 100 !== 0 || year % 400 === 0);
  const days = [31, leap ? 29 : 28, 31, 30, 31, 30, 31, 31, 30, 31, 30, 31];
  return day >= 1 && day <= days[month - 1];
}

const priorities = ['Low', 'Normal', 'High'];
const isObject = (value) => value !== null && typeof value === 'object' && !Array.isArray(value);
const nonblankString = (value) => typeof value === 'string' && value.trim().length > 0;

function validateProjectJSON(text) {
  let document;
  try { document = JSON.parse(text); } catch { return null; }
  if (!isObject(document) || document.format !== 'workboard-project' || document.version !== 1) return null;
  const project = document.project;
  if (!isObject(project) || !nonblankString(project.name) || typeof project.archived !== 'boolean' ||
      !priorities.includes(project.defaultPriority) || !Array.isArray(project.tasks)) return null;
  for (const task of project.tasks) {
    if (!isObject(task) || !nonblankString(task.title) || typeof task.completed !== 'boolean' ||
        !priorities.includes(task.priority) || typeof task.dueDate !== 'string' ||
        (task.dueDate !== '' && !validDueDate(task.dueDate)) || typeof task.notes !== 'string' ||
        typeof task.deleted !== 'boolean') return null;
  }
  return project;
}

const insertImportedProject = db.prepare('INSERT INTO projects (name, archived, default_priority) VALUES (?, ?, ?)');
const insertImportedTask = db.prepare(`INSERT INTO tasks
  (project_id, title, completed, priority, due_date, notes, deleted, position)
  VALUES (?, ?, ?, ?, ?, ?, ?, ?)`);

function importProject(name, project) {
  let projectId;
  transaction(() => {
    projectId = insertImportedProject.run(name, Number(project.archived), project.defaultPriority).lastInsertRowid;
    project.tasks.forEach((task, index) => {
      const position = index + 1;
      const taskId = insertImportedTask.run(projectId, task.title, Number(task.completed), task.priority,
        task.dueDate, task.notes.replace(/\r\n?/g, '\n'), Number(task.deleted), position).lastInsertRowid;
      rememberPosition.run(taskId, projectId, position);
    });
  });
  return projectId;
}

const taskFilter = (value) => ['Open', 'Completed', 'Deleted'].includes(value) ? value : 'All';
const priorityFilter = (value) => priorities.includes(value) ? value : 'All';
function dueRange(values) {
  const from = (values.get('dueFrom') || '').trim();
  const through = (values.get('dueThrough') || '').trim();
  if ((from && !validDueDate(from)) || (through && !validDueDate(through)) ||
      (from && through && from > through)) return { from: '', through: '' };
  return { from, through };
}

// Normalize only for matching; stored names/titles and displayed queries stay intact.
const searchQuery = (values) => (values.get('searchQuery') || '').trim();
const normalizeSearch = (value) => value.replace(/[ \t]+/g, ' ')
  .replace(/[A-Z]/g, (letter) => letter.toLowerCase());
const matchesSearch = (value, query) => normalizeSearch(value).includes(normalizeSearch(query));

const projectFilter = (value) => value === 'Archived' ? 'Archived' : 'Active';

const escapeHtml = (value) => String(value).replace(/[&<>"']/g, (char) => ({
  '&': '&amp;', '<': '&lt;', '>': '&gt;', '"': '&quot;', "'": '&#39;',
}[char]));

function page(title, content) {
  return `<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
  <meta charset="utf-8">
  <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1">
  <title>${escapeHtml(title)} · Workboard</title>
  <style>
    :root { font-family: system-ui, sans-serif; color: #172b42; background: #f4f6fa; }
    * { box-sizing: border-box; }
    body { margin: 0; }
    main { max-width: 760px; margin: 64px auto; padding: 0 24px; }
    h1 { font-size: 36px; letter-spacing: -1px; overflow-wrap: anywhere; }
    .intro { color: #526174; margin-bottom: 32px; }
    .panel, .project { background: white; border: 1px solid #dce2eb; border-radius: 12px; padding: 24px; }
    .rename { margin-bottom: 20px; }
    label { display: block; font-weight: 600; margin-bottom: 8px; }
    .fields { display: flex; gap: 12px; }
    input { min-width: 0; flex: 1; border: 1px solid #8492a6; border-radius: 6px; padding: 12px; font: inherit; }
    textarea { display: block; width: 100%; min-height: 110px; resize: vertical; border: 1px solid #8492a6; border-radius: 6px; padding: 12px; font: inherit; margin-bottom: 12px; }
    button { font: inherit; font-weight: 600; border: 0; border-radius: 6px; padding: 12px 18px; background: #234fc4; color: white; cursor: pointer; }
    button:hover { background: #193c99; }
    button:disabled { background: #8492a6; cursor: not-allowed; }
    :focus-visible { outline: 3px solid #b36b00; outline-offset: 3px; }
    .projects { display: grid; gap: 12px; margin-top: 28px; }
    .project { display: flex; align-items: center; justify-content: space-between; gap: 20px; }
    .project-name { font-weight: 600; overflow-wrap: anywhere; min-width: 0; }
    .project form { flex-shrink: 0; }
    .project-actions { display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: 8px; }
    .summary { color: #526174; margin: 8px 0 0; }
    .empty { color: #526174; }
    .filter { margin-top: 28px; }
    select { font: inherit; padding: 10px; border: 1px solid #8492a6; border-radius: 6px; background: white; }
    .task { background: white; border: 1px solid #dce2eb; border-radius: 12px; padding: 20px; }
    .task .completion-label { display: flex; align-items: center; gap: 12px; margin: 0; overflow-wrap: anywhere; }
    .task input[type="checkbox"] { flex: none; width: 20px; height: 20px; }
    .task-rename { margin-top: 20px; }
    [role="alert"] { color: #9c2222; background: #fff0f0; padding: 12px; border-radius: 6px; }
    @media (max-width: 520px) { main { margin-top: 32px; } .fields, .project { flex-direction: column; align-items: stretch; } }
  </style>
</head>
<body><main>${content}</main></body>
</html>`;
}

function projectsPage(error = '', filter = 'Active', search = '', importDraft = { json: '', name: '', error: '' }) {
  const projects = listProjects.all(filter === 'Archived' ? 1 : 0).filter((project) => matchesSearch(project.name, search));
  const searchField = `<input type="hidden" name="searchQuery" value="${escapeHtml(search)}">`;
  return page('Projects', `<h1>Workboard</h1>
    <p class="intro">A place for your projects.</p>
    <form method="get" action="/directory"><button type="submit">Task directory</button></form>
    <form class="panel" method="post" action="/projects">
      ${searchField}
      <input type="hidden" name="filter" value="${filter}">
      <label for="project-name">Project name</label>
      <div class="fields"><input id="project-name" name="name" type="text" autocomplete="off"><button type="submit">Create project</button></div>
      ${error ? `<p role="alert">${escapeHtml(error)}</p>` : ''}
    </form>
    <form class="panel filter" method="post" action="/projects/import">
      ${searchField}
      <input type="hidden" name="filter" value="${filter}">
      <label for="project-json">Project JSON</label>

import test from 'node:test';
import assert from 'node:assert/strict';
import { spawn } from 'node:child_process';
import { once } from 'node:events';
import { mkdtemp, rm } from 'node:fs/promises';
import { tmpdir } from 'node:os';
import { join } from 'node:path';
import { DatabaseSync } from 'node:sqlite';

test('directory ordering is stable across owners, retained by actions, and never changes stored positions', async () => {
  const dir = await mkdtemp(join(tmpdir(), 'workboard-directory-order-'));
  const dbPath = join(dir, 'workboard.sqlite');
  let app;
  try {
    app = await launch(dbPath);
    const post = (path, fields = {}) => fetch(app.url + path, {
      method: 'POST', body: new URLSearchParams(fields), redirect: 'manual',
    });
    const get = async (path) => (await fetch(app.url + path)).text();
    const titles = (html) => [...html.matchAll(/data-testid="directory-task-title"[^>]*>([^<]*)<\/h2>/g)].map((m) => m[1]);
    const pathFor = (fields) => '/directory?' + new URLSearchParams(fields);
    const snapshot = () => {
      const db = new DatabaseSync(dbPath);
      try { return ['projects', 'tasks', 'task_positions'].map((table) => db.prepare(`SELECT * FROM ${table} ORDER BY rowid`).all()); }
      finally { db.close(); }
    };
    const task = (title, priority, dueDate) => ({ title, priority, dueDate,
      completed: false, notes: ' literal\n雪 ', deleted: false });
    const first = [task('Zebra', 'Low', ''), task('alpha', 'High', '2025-01-01'),
      task('a  b', 'Normal', '0001-01-01'), task('\u{10000}', 'Normal', '')];
    const second = [task('ALPHA', 'High', '2025-01-01'), task('a b', 'Low', '9999-12-31'),
      task('\ue000', 'Normal', '')];
    for (const [name, tasks] of [['First', first], ['Second', second]]) {
      const document = { format: 'workboard-project', version: 1,
        project: { name, archived: false, defaultPriority: 'Normal', tasks } };
      await post('/projects/import', { name, json: JSON.stringify(document) });
    }
    const original = [...first, ...second].map((task) => task.title);
    const expected = {
      Original: original,
      Priority: ['alpha', 'ALPHA', 'a  b', '\u{10000}', '\ue000', 'Zebra', 'a b'],
      'Due date': ['a  b', 'alpha', 'ALPHA', 'a b', 'Zebra', '\u{10000}', '\ue000'],
      Title: ['a  b', 'a b', 'alpha', 'ALPHA', 'Zebra', '\ue000', '\u{10000}'],
    };
    const before = snapshot();
    const exportBefore = await (await fetch(app.url + '/projects/1/download')).json();
    const initial = await get('/directory');
    const options = initial.match(/<select id="directory-order"[^>]*>([\s\S]*?)<\/select>/)[1];
    assert.deepEqual([...options.matchAll(/<option(?: selected)?>([^<]*)<\/option>/g)].map((m) => m[1]), Object.keys(expected));
    assert.match(initial, /<label for="directory-order">Directory order<\/label>/);
    assert.match(options, /<option selected>Original/);
    for (const [order, names] of Object.entries(expected)) {
      assert.deepEqual(titles(await get(pathFor({ order }))), names);
    }
    assert.deepEqual(titles(await get('/directory?order=unknown')), original);
    assert.deepEqual(snapshot(), before);
    assert.deepEqual(await (await fetch(app.url + '/projects/1/download')).json(), exportBefore);
    assert.deepEqual([... (await get('/projects/1')).matchAll(/<span>([^<]*)<\/span>/g)].map((m) => m[1]), first.map((t) => t.title));

    const selected = { scope: 'Active', filter: 'Open', priorityFilter: 'High',
      dueFrom: '2025-01-01', dueThrough: '2025-01-01', searchQuery: 'alpha', order: 'Title' };
    const html = await get(pathFor(selected));
    assert.deepEqual(titles(html), ['alpha', 'ALPHA']);
    assert.equal([...html.matchAll(/name="order" value="Title"/g)].length, 3);
    for (const [path, extra] of [
      ['/directory/search', { query: ' ALPHA ' }],
      ['/directory/due-range', { rangeFrom: '2025-01-01', rangeThrough: '2025-01-01' }],
    ]) {
      const response = await post(path, { ...selected, ...extra });
      const location = new URL(response.headers.get('location'), app.url);
      for (const key of ['scope', 'filter', 'priorityFilter', 'dueFrom', 'dueThrough', 'order']) {
        if (key !== 'scope') assert.equal(location.searchParams.get(key), selected[key]);
      }
      assert.deepEqual(titles(await get(location.pathname + location.search)), ['alpha', 'ALPHA']);
    }
    const invalid = await post('/directory/due-range', { ...selected, rangeFrom: '2025-02-29' });
    assert.equal(invalid.status, 422);
    const invalidHtml = await invalid.text();
    assert.match(invalidHtml, /<option selected>Title/);
    assert.deepEqual(titles(invalidHtml), ['alpha', 'ALPHA']);
    assert.deepEqual(snapshot(), before);
    const complete = await post('/directory/completion', { ...selected, completed: '1' });
    const completedLocation = new URL(complete.headers.get('location'), app.url);
